                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dd179d5-8e98-451f-8df3-9479b7d068fd",
                                "sense_id": "9c523e8a-a452-327d-bb33-9ba3c126174f",
                                "text": "As with favorites, you can unreject a rejected selection by selecting it and then clicking the Unmark Selection button I just mentioned."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53c0dbaa-88e2-48a3-ab38-7892ec445eb5",
                                "sense_id": "9c523e8a-a452-327d-bb33-9ba3c126174f",
                                "text": "If you want to unreject an image, select it and set its rating to something other than rejected, be it unrated or one to five stars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b867843-1066-4922-9871-2db26517cb5b",
                                "sense_id": "9c523e8a-a452-327d-bb33-9ba3c126174f",
                                "text": "Karlan and Zinman, the ones who later wrote “Lying about Borrowing,” persuaded lenders in South Africa and the Philippines to randomly “unreject” some people who had applied for loans. No one was randomly rejected."
                            }
